        The shop's link name (current or former).

        + Sample: raptorrush

### addPhotos [POST]
Adds one or more photos after the cover. Each is turned upright, resized to at most 2000 px and stored as WebP. A shop holds up to 8 photos; buyers swipe through them on the shop page. Not for recommendations, which show the retailer's photos.
+ Attributes
    + photo (string, required)

        An image, up to 15 MB. The endpoint also accepts the field repeated, to add several in one request.


+ Request (multipart/form-data)




+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The shop's photos, cover first.

    + Attributes (ShopPhotos)



+ Response 400 (application/json)

        Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.

    + Attributes (Error)



+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (Error)



### setPhotoOrder [PUT]
Sets the photo order; the first becomes the cover. Leaving a photo out removes it.

+ Request (<<Add Header Value>>)

    + Attributes (Api Shops Photos Request)



+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The shop's photos, cover first.

    + Attributes (ShopPhotos)



+ Response 400 (application/json)

        Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.

    + Attributes (Error)



+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (Error)





# Group Links

Short shop links (`/<slug>`).

## Api Slugs Check [/api/slugs/check{?name}]

### checkLinkName [GET]
Normalises a proposed link name and says whether a new shop can use it.
+ Parameters
    + name (string, required)

        Anything; it is normalised (`Raptor Rush` becomes `raptor-rush`).


+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The normalised name and whether it can be used.

    + Attributes (Api Slugs Check Response)





# Group Products

Find products to recommend (Channel3 catalog).

## Api Channel3 Search [/api/channel3/search{?q}]

### searchProducts [GET]
Searches 100M+ products from 25k+ stores through Channel3. Pass a result's `id` to `createShop` with `source=channel3`.
+ Parameters
    + q (string, required)

        What to look for, in plain words.

        + Sample: gifts for trail runners under $60

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        Up to 12 products.

    + Attributes (Api Channel3 Search Response)



+ Response 502 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (Error)



+ Response 503 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (Error)





# Group Checkout

Buyer-side PayPal checkout.

## Api Paypal Client Token [/api/paypal/client-token]

### getPayPalClientToken [GET]
A browser-safe client token for the PayPal JavaScript SDK v6
(`paypal.createInstance({ clientToken })`), bound to the requesting site's domain.
Shop pages call this before showing the PayPal button.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        A token for this site's domain.

    + Attributes (Api Paypal Client Token Response)



+ Response 502 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (Error)



+ Response 503 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (Error)




## Api Orders [/api/orders]

### createCheckoutOrder [POST]
Creates the PayPal order for one unit of a live shop's product. The amount always comes
from the shop, never from the caller. Pass the returned `id` to the PayPal JS SDK.

+ Request (<<Add Header Value>>)

    + Attributes (Api Orders Request)



+ Response 200 (application/json)

        PayPal order created.

    + Attributes (Api Orders Response)



+ Response 400 (application/json)

        Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.

    + Attributes (Error)



+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (Error)



+ Response 409 (application/json)

        Taken or unavailable (a link name, or a sold-out product).

    + Attributes (Error)



+ Response 502 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (Error)



+ Response 503 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (Error)




## Api Orders Capture By PaypalOrderId [/api/orders/{paypalOrderId}/capture]

+ Parameters
    + paypalOrderId (string, required)

        The PayPal order id that `createCheckoutOrder` returned.


### captureCheckoutOrder [POST]
Call after the buyer approves. Records the sale; digital orders get a download link or access code.
Safe to call repeatedly: before approval it answers 409, so a page can poll it while the PayPal window is open.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        Paid.

    + Attributes (Api Orders Capture Response)



+ Response 402 (application/json)

        Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.

    + Attributes (Error)



+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (Error)



+ Response 409 (application/json)

        The buyer hasn't approved the order yet.

    + Attributes (Api Orders Capture 409 Error1)



+ Response 422 (application/json)

        The buyer's funding source was declined (`INSTRUMENT_DECLINED`); they can try another.

    + Attributes (Error)



+ Response 502 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (Error)





# Group Access codes

Unlock a paid app or game with a buyer's code.

## Api Access Verify [/api/access/verify]

### verifyAccessCode [POST]
For apps and games sold with access codes. Callable from any origin (CORS `*`): it only
answers valid or not for one shop, and counts uses. Accepts the shop's current or former
link names, and codes typed loosely (lower case, spaces, no dashes).

+ Request (<<Add Header Value>>)

    + Attributes (Api Access Verify Request)



+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The answer. Invalid codes are also a 200.

    + Attributes (Api Access Verify Response)





